{
  "configuration_id": "config_009",
  "reason": "The current best is config_047 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted, acc=0.706). The evidence strongly supports scvi_n200 as the best RNA encoder, imagenet_vit_l as the best image encoder, and weighted fusion. The main uncertainty is whether transformer aggregation could outperform avgpool when paired with the richer scvi_n200 representations. Previous evidence against transformer (config_032: 0.573 vs config_010: 0.639) was obtained with the weaker pca_n2000 encoder; scvi_n200's more structured, high-dimensional latent space may benefit from the attention-based interactions that transformer aggregation captures, which a simple average would discard. This experiment tests that specific hypothesis while keeping all other components at their proven-best settings. Expected cost is moderate (~5-7 GPU hours), comparable to config_047's 4.82 hours plus a small transformer overhead, keeping total budget well within reasonable bounds. With only 1 experiment remaining after this, testing the single most uncertain design axis (aggregation) with the strongest encoder combination is the highest-value use of the slot."
}

